<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14441" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπρονό-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unpremeditated,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρασία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>MM</u>
					1203a30
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χώρα ἀ.</span> an
			<i>unguarded</i> country, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.5.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόποι ἀ.</span>”
				<i>unreconnoitred,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					3.48.4
				</span></i>
			; <i>not the work of providence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόσμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.411
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				11p.442M.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not considering beforehand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὀργὴ -τον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.3.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἀπαράσκευοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					5.7.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				233
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῶν ἐσομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>Vit.</u>
					13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἐπὶ γῆς πραγμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
				</span></i>
			<i>Bis Acc.</i><i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, etc.; of the gods, <i>not exercising providence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				368
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					1.4.21
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινὸς ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.5.1
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προνοίᾳ,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.151
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀ. θεώμενοι</span>”
				<i>without previous acquaintance,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					10.14.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
